From 8aec614e5c05599818cf3689a2139d85bce990dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Edward Hervey <edward@centricular.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:57:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] parsebin: wait for the parser to publish its stream-id before
 exposing

A chain was declared complete as soon as a parser was plugged, since
chain->parsed is set at plug time. Parsers create their stream-id
lazily, on the first data they push, so the exposed pad published a
stream-collection built from an earlier stream-start and then emitted a
different one. decodebin3 could not find a collection covering the
stream and aborted in mq_slot_handle_stream_start().

Require the endpad target to have published a stream-id before rule (c)
declares the chain complete. Exposure then happens from the block probe
on that target, once it has produced events, so the collection and the
stream-start agree by construction.

Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/merge_requests/12700>
---
 .../gst-plugins-base/gst/playback/gstparsebin.c    | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gst/playback/gstparsebin.c b/gst/playback/gstparsebin.c
index 535f91a8bf9..3d073932297 100644
--- a/gst/playback/gstparsebin.c
+++ b/gst/playback/gstparsebin.c
@@ -3148,9 +3148,17 @@ gst_parse_chain_is_complete (GstParseChain * chain)
     }
   }
 
-  if (chain->parsed) {
-    complete = TRUE;
-    goto out;
+  if (chain->parsed && chain->endpad) {
+    /* Plugging a parser is not enough to expose: the parser creates its
+     * stream-id lazily, on the first data it pushes, so a pad exposed here
+     * would publish a stream-collection built from an earlier stream-start
+     * and then emit a different one. The ghost mirrors its target's sticky
+     * events, so wait until the pad we are about to publish knows its own
+     * identity; the block probe on the target triggers exposure once it does. */
+    gchar *sid = gst_pad_get_stream_id (GST_PAD (chain->endpad));
+
+    complete = (sid != NULL);
+    g_free (sid);
   }
 
 out:
